  "statementTechnical": "The entity satisfying all boundary conditions (BC1-BC8), when equipped with PERSONHOOD (agency, intentionality, relational capacity), is identical to the transcendent agent denominated \"God.\" [NOTE: Structural property-matching alone doesn't make something a person. A mathematical object could satisfy all boundary conditions without being God. Personhood properties are required — see new PERSONHOOD axiom.]",
  "statementPlain": "The entity satisfying all boundary conditions (BC1-BC8), when equipped with PERSONHOOD (agency, intentionality, relational capacity), is identical to the transcendent agent denominated \"God.\" [NOTE: Structural property-matching alone doesn't make something a person. A mathematical object could satisfy all boundary conditions without being God. Personhood properties are required — see new PERSONHOOD axiom.]",
  "mathematicalForm": "TO ≡ G; BC1∧BC2∧BC3∧BC4∧BC5∧BC6∧BC7∧BC8 → unique(TO)",
